I now have a complete picture of how assets flow through every layer. Here is the thorough report.

---

# Asset flow in the Pathland protocol — full layer-by-layer map

## 1. IMAGE component + IMAGE_SOURCE (0x1002)

### 1a. Protocol core — `lib/rust/crates/pathland-core/src/constants.rs`

Component declaration (line 209):
```rust
/// Raster, vector, or system icon asset.
pub const IMAGE: u16 = 0x02;
```

Property declaration (line 329–330):
```rust
/// **Draft.** Image source (STRING: a resource name, file path, or URL).
pub const IMAGE_SOURCE: u16 = 0x1002;
```

The spec comment on `IMAGE` (constants.rs:208) reads *"Raster, vector, or system icon asset"* — the protocol's notion of an asset today is a single STRING reference. There is **no binary payload path** — assets are always identified by name/path/URL and loaded client-side ("Asset loading is client-owned", `spec/PRIMITIVES.md:248`).

### 1b. HTML renderer (SSR) — `lib/rust/crates/pathland-render-html/src/lib.rs`

The IMAGE arm is at lines 984–992:
```rust
component_type::IMAGE => {
    let src = escape(
        node.strings
            .get(&property_id::IMAGE_SOURCE)
            .map(String::as_str)
            .unwrap_or_default(),
    );
    format!("<img{data_id}{event}{aria} src=\"{src}\"{style}>")
}
```

Key observations:
- `IMAGE_SOURCE` is resolved from `node.strings` — the STRING-typed properties map populated in `apply_style` when a `SET_PROPERTY` carries `value_type::STRING` (lib.rs:755–772). Only `src` is emitted; **there is no `alt=` attribute** (see §6).
- The `{style}` is `Node::style_css()` + `border_style()`. Notably, `style_css()` (lib.rs:122–391) contains **no `CONTENT_MODE` / `ASPECT_RATIO` handling** — the Rust SSR does not emit `object-fit` or `aspect-ratio` for images (the TS client does; see §2).
- The `size_css()` helper (lib.rs:452–460) is what WIDTH/HEIGHT use:
```rust
fn size_css(v: f32) -> String {
    if v == pathland_core::size::FILL {
        "100%".to_string()
    } else if v == pathland_core::size::HUG_CONTENT {
        "fit-content".to_string()
    } else {
        format!("{v}px")
    }
}
```
- WIDTH/HEIGHT are applied in `style_css` (lib.rs:181–194); `HUG_CONTENT` is skipped (left to intrinsic size), `FILL` → `100%`.
- The golden test `renders_image_with_source` (lib.rs:1660–1681) asserts the exact output:
```rust
assert!(html.contains("<img data-pathland-id=\"1\" src=\"assets/logo.png\">"));
```
It drives a `CREATE_NODE(component=IMAGE)` + `SET_PROPERTY` with `((value_type::STRING as u32) << 16) | property_id::IMAGE_SOURCE`.

The global CSS reset also has image rules (`css.rs:51–52`):
```css
img, svg, video, canvas, audio, iframe, embed, object { display: block; vertical-align: middle; }
img, video { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
```
(The `video`/`audio` here are just generic UA-reset selectors — no media components exist.)

### 1c. TS DOM client — `lib/typescript/src/{elements,apply,classes}.ts`

**Image shell** — `elements.ts:77–81`:
```ts
case COMPONENT_IMAGE: {
  const el = document.createElement("img");
  el.alt = "";
  return el;
}
```
`alt` is hard-coded empty at shell creation; nothing ever sets it later.

**IMAGE_SOURCE apply** — `apply.ts:601–607` (in `applyStringProperty`, reached for `VAL_STRING` properties via `applyStyle` → `CMD_SET_PROPERTY`):
```ts
case PROP_IMAGE_SOURCE: {
  const img = el.matches("img") ? el : el.querySelector("img");
  if (img instanceof HTMLImageElement) {
    img.src = text;
  }
  break;
}
```
On hydration (`index.ts:101–107`) the client collects the SSR `<img>` elements by `data-pathland-id` and does **not** re-apply string props — the SSR `src` is trusted; only later deltas update it.

**CONTENT_MODE objectFit** — `classes.ts:320–323`:
```ts
[P.PROP_ASPECT_RATIO]: (el, vt, c) => (el.style.aspectRatio = fmtFloat(f32(vt, c))),
[P.PROP_CONTENT_MODE]: (el, vt, c) => {
  el.style.objectFit = enumCode(vt, c) === P.CONTENT_MODE_FILL ? "fill" : "contain";
},
```
Note the asymmetry: `Fit` → `object-fit: contain`, `Fill` → `object-fit: fill` (not `cover`).

**WIDTH/HEIGHT sizing** — `classes.ts:467–480`:
```ts
[P.PROP_WIDTH]: (el, vt, c) => {
  const v = f32(vt, c);
  if (v !== P.WIDTH_HUG) {
    el.style.width = sizeCss(v);
  }
},
[P.PROP_HEIGHT]: (el, vt, c) => {
  const v = f32(vt, c);
  if (v !== P.WIDTH_HUG) {
    el.style.height = sizeCss(v);
  }
},
```
with `sizeCss` (classes.ts:582–590):
```ts
export function sizeCss(value: number): string {
  if (value === P.WIDTH_FILL) return "100%";
  if (value === P.WIDTH_HUG) return "fit-content";
  return fmtFloat(value) + "px";
}
```

TS constants (`constants.ts`, generated by `pathland-ts-codegen`): `PROP_IMAGE_SOURCE = 0x1002` (line 112), `PROP_CONTENT_MODE = 0x001c` (109), `PROP_ASPECT_RATIO = 0x001b` (108), `COMPONENT_IMAGE = 0x0002` (294), `CONTENT_MODE_FIT = 0` / `CONTENT_MODE_FILL = 1` (215–216), `WIDTH_FILL = -1` / `WIDTH_HUG = -2` (187–188).

### 1d. GTK renderer — `lib/rust/crates/pathland-render-gtk/src/lib.rs`

Widget kind mapping — `lib.rs:754–755`:
```rust
/// `IMAGE` → `GtkPicture`.
Image,
```
`widget_kind()` — `lib.rs:803`:
```rust
component_type::IMAGE => WidgetKind::Image,
```
Widget construction — `lib.rs:962`:
```rust
WidgetKind::Image => gtk::Picture::new().upcast(),
```
Property application — `lib.rs:321–327`:
```rust
WidgetKind::Image => {
    if let Ok(pic) = widget.downcast::<gtk::Picture>() {
        if let Some(src) = node.string_property(property_id::IMAGE_SOURCE) {
            pic.set_filename(Some(src));
        }
    }
}
```

Critical caveats for your planning:
- `GtkPicture::set_filename` requires a **local filesystem path** — a URL or a bare resource name (`icons/home.svg`) will **not** load through this call today. There is no URL-loading, no `GtkImage`, no bytes-from-memory path.
- The GTK renderer does **not** handle `CONTENT_MODE` or `ASPECT_RATIO` for images at all (grep for `CONTENT_MODE|ASPECT_RATIO` in the GTK crate returns nothing). Only WIDTH/HEIGHT sizing is generic via `apply_style` → `size_hint` (see §2).
- The host-side STRING resolution is proven in `host.rs:535–567` (`string_properties_resolve_from_frame`): a guest writes `create_node(1, IMAGE)` + `set_property(1, IMAGE_SOURCE, STRING, ref_src)` and the host resolves `n.string_property(IMAGE_SOURCE) == Some("assets/logo.png")`, with the raw arena offset *not* stored in `properties`.

### 1e. Java DSL — `lib/java/pathland-view/src/main/java/com/pathland/view/Image.java`

Full file (46 lines):
```java
/** An image leaf (a native element; the renderer resolves the visual). */
public final class Image implements View {

    private final String source;
    private final Signal<String> sourceSignal;

    private Image(String source, Signal<String> sourceSignal) {
        this.source = source;
        this.sourceSignal = sourceSignal;
    }

    /** An image with no source (the renderer's default visual). */
    public static Image of() { return new Image(null, null); }

    /** An image with a source (resource name, file path, or absolute URL). */
    public static Image of(String source) { return new Image(source, null); }

    /**
     * An image whose source is bound to a reactive signal: a change re-emits only this
     * node's {@code IMAGE_SOURCE}.
     */
    public static Image of(Signal<String> source) { return new Image(null, source); }

    @Override
    public PathlandNode render(Environment env) {
        PathlandNode node = new PathlandNode(Components.IMAGE);
        if (sourceSignal != null) {
            node.properties.put(Properties.IMAGE_SOURCE, sourceSignal.get());
            node.propertyBindings.put(Properties.IMAGE_SOURCE, sourceSignal);
        } else if (source != null) {
            node.properties.put(Properties.IMAGE_SOURCE, source);
        }
        return node;
    }
}
```
The signal overload registers a node-level binding effect so a source change re-emits only that node's `IMAGE_SOURCE` `SET_PROPERTY`.

Companion Java types:
- `Components.IMAGE = 0x02` (`Components.java:14`); `Properties.IMAGE_SOURCE = 0x1002` (`Properties.java:36`).
- `ImageSource.java` — a chainable `ViewModifier` that sets `IMAGE_SOURCE` (`Modified.prop(Properties.IMAGE_SOURCE, value)`, line 20).
- `ContentMode.java` — enum `FIT(0)`, `FILL(1)`.
- `AspectRatio.java` — emits `ASPECT_RATIO` + `CONTENT_MODE` (lines 22–24).
- `ScaledToFit.java` / `ScaledToFill.java` — emit `CONTENT_MODE=Fit` / `CONTENT_MODE=Fill`.

### 1f. Rust DSL (pathland-view) — `lib/rust/crates/pathland-view/src/lib.rs:895–902`

```rust
/// An image view (`IMAGE_SOURCE` is a future STRING property).
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq)]
pub struct Image;
impl View for Image {
    fn build(&self) -> Node {
        plain_node(Component::Image, Vec::new(), BTreeMap::new())
    }
}
```
The Rust DSL has only a placeholder `Image` with **no source argument** — the STRING property is explicitly "future". The GTK demo never uses it (grep for `Image` in `pathland-render-gtk-demo` returns nothing).

---

## 2. CONTENT_MODE (0x001C), ASPECT_RATIO (0x001B), WIDTH/HEIGHT FILL/HUG sizing as applied to images

| Layer | CONTENT_MODE | ASPECT_RATIO | WIDTH/HEIGHT FILL/HUG |
|---|---|---|---|
| Core constants | `CONTENT_MODE = 0x001C` (constants.rs:324), F32 enum `Fit`=0 / `Fill`=1; value type `F32` (default arm, constants.rs:529) | `ASPECT_RATIO = 0x001B` (constants.rs:322), F32 | `size::FILL = -1.0`, `size::HUG_CONTENT = -2.0` (constants.rs:534–539) |
| Rust HTML SSR | **Not rendered** — no `object-fit` emitted | **Not rendered** — no `aspect-ratio` emitted | `style_css` (lib.rs:181–194) via `size_css`: FILL → `100%`, HUG → omitted, else px |
| TS DOM client | `classes.ts:321–323` → `el.style.objectFit = enumCode === CONTENT_MODE_FILL ? "fill" : "contain"` | `classes.ts:320` → `el.style.aspectRatio` | `classes.ts:467–480` + `sizeCss` (582–590): FILL → `100%`, HUG → `fit-content`, else px |
| GTK | **Not handled** | **Not handled** | Generic `apply_style` (lib.rs:1305–1345): `size_hint` (1293–1300) maps FILL → `set_hexpand/set_vexpand(true)` + `Align::Fill`; fixed → `set_size_request`; HUG/absent → natural size |
| Java DSL | `AspectRatio.of(ratio, mode)` emits `CONTENT_MODE` as F32 (AspectRatio.java:22–24); `ScaledToFit`/`ScaledToFill` emit it | `AspectRatio.of` emits `ASPECT_RATIO` F32 | `FrameMod` (generic) |

The `debug.rs` pretty-printer names them (`debug.rs:83–84`, and `CONTENT_MODE` enum decode at `debug.rs:277–281`), but they are render-dead in the SSR and GTK paths. **Only the TS DOM client actually interprets `CONTENT_MODE`/`ASPECT_RATIO` visually** (and only via runtime deltas — the SSR `<img>` gets no `object-fit`/`aspect-ratio` inline style, so an image rendered server-side and hydrated with no delta shows no content-mode).

