## 3. How the demos serve asset bytes

**The short answer: they don't.** No SVG (or any image) file exists anywhere in the repository:

```
find ... -name "*.svg"  → (no output)
```

The demo views reference icons as **relative URLs** — but the bytes are never provided:

`lib/java/pathland-demo-views/src/main/java/com/pathland/demo/sidebar/Sidebar.java:26–28`:
```java
menuRow("/home", "Home", "icons/home.svg"),
menuRow("/kitchen", "Kitchen sink", "icons/kitchen.svg"),
menuRow("/settings", "Settings", "icons/settings.svg"),
```
(and `menuRow` builds `Label.of(label, icon)` at line 59, `Button.of(...)` at 58–61).

`lib/java/pathland-demo-views/src/main/java/com/pathland/demo/kitchensink/LabelSection.java:26–32`:
```java
Label.of("Settings", "icons/settings.svg"),
Label.of("Save changes", "icons/save.svg"),
...
Label.of("Cloud", "icons/cloud.svg")
Label.of(status.signal(), "icons/status.svg"),
```
The comment at `LabelSection.java:16` is explicit: *"Icon sources are illustrative — the renderer resolves them."*

What each demo **does** serve:

- **Quarkus demo** — resources are only `application.properties` and `META-INF/resources/pathland-dom-renderer.js`. Quarkus serves `META-INF/resources/**` as static content automatically. The starter's catch-all `IndexResource` (`{path:(?!ws).*}`) explicitly relies on this — `IndexResource.java:40–41`: *"Quarkus serves the static JS bundle from `META-INF/resources` before JAX-RS, so it is not shadowed."* So an `icons/*.svg` placed at `src/main/resources/META-INF/resources/icons/` would be served at `/icons/*.svg` automatically. The icons are simply absent.
- **Spring Boot demo** — resources are `application.properties` and `static/pathland-dom-renderer.js` (Spring Boot serves `static/**` automatically). The starter additionally has an explicit controller for the one known asset because the `/{*path}` catch-all would shadow it — `PathlandIndexController.java:60–71`:
```java
/**
 * The single static asset — served explicitly so the /{*path} catch-all never
 * shadows it. Built by lib/typescript and copied into the app's src/main/resources/static.
 */
@GetMapping(value = "/pathland-dom-renderer.js", produces = "application/javascript")
@ResponseBody
public byte[] bundle() throws IOException {
    try (InputStream in = new ClassPathResource("static/pathland-dom-renderer.js").getInputStream()) {
        return in.readAllBytes();
    }
}
```
The same `/{*path}` catch-all (`PathlandIndexController.java:43`) would also shadow `icons/*.svg`, so the Spring path would need an explicit exemption or a static-resource handler for icons — **another gap** if you add real icon files.

**No controller anywhere serves image bytes**, and no `Image.of(...)`-style usage exists outside `Label` (grep for `Image.of` in demo-views returns nothing — all icon usage goes through `Label`).

